 "title": "Services | Sherburne County, MN",
 "text": "Services | Sherburne County, MN\nLoading\nSkip to Main Content\nCreate a Website Account - Manage notification subscriptions, save form progress and more.\nWebsite Sign In\nSearch\nHow Do I...\nYour Government\nServices\nDoing Business\nHome\nServices\nServices\nSherburne County Mission\nTo provide the necessary services in a cost effective manner to support quality of life for Sherburne County citizens.\n9\n1\n1\n2\nCitizen eServices\nAccess links to local resources such as beacons, CodeRED, and other online services.\nCommunity Indicators\nCommunity Indicators\nCounty Attorney\nSherburne County -- County-Attorney\nDirections & Facilities\nSee directions and a map to our facility or see our department listings.\nDo I Live in Sherburne?\nSelect your geography to see if you live within the county.\nEmergencies\nHere you will find information for responding to and preparing for emergencies including natural disasters, personal / medical emergencies, and acts of terrorism. If you have an emergency now, call 911.\nEnvironment\nThe Environmental Subdivision of the Zoning Administration department aims to provide information and services for the well-being of Sherburne County's general public with regard to land use and water.\nHealth & Human Services\nJudicial Services\nFind links to court administration, Community Corrections, jury duty, or the law library.\nLaw Enforcement\nView child protection services, community corrections, community programs, jail information, and juvenile diversion information.\nLiving Here\nFor our residents, we have selected information about driver's licenses, transportation, recycling, voting, and education.\nPublic Records\nHere you can access birth and death records, marriage certificates, military discharge records, passports and real estate information.\nVeterans Services\nSherburne County Veteran Services provides responsive, accurate and compassionate assistance to veterans, their dependents and survivors in applying for applicable federal, state, county and military benefits.\nVisiting\nLearn about upcoming events, find the nearest fishing lake, or use our maps to find your way around the county. We hope you enjoy your stay!\nCitizen eServices\nBeacon Property Information\nPrint Tax Statement\nRoad Construction Viewer\nPublic Works Report a Concern\nHyper-Reach Alert Notifications\nCommunity Indicators\nCounty Attorney\nDirections & Facilities\nDo I Live in Sherburne?\nEmergencies\nDisaster Response\nEmergency Preparedness\nFamily Financial Assistance\nLaw Enforcement\nViolence & Abuse\nEnvironment\nHealth & Human Services\nFinancial & Health Care Assistance\nChild & Family Services\nAdult Services\nHealthy Communities\nJudicial Services\nCommunity Corrections\nCourt Administration\nJury Duty\nLaw Library\nPublic Court Calendar (PDF)\nLaw Enforcement\nChild Protection Services\nCommunity Corrections\nCommunity Programs\nJail & Facilities\nLiving Here\nAbout Us\nAddress Information\nCounty Libraries\nCounty Wide Fee Schedule\nDriver's License\nProperty Information\nProperty Taxes\nPublic Transportation\nThe Northstar Line\nPublic Works Transportation Division\nTri-CAP Transportation\nTrash & Recycling\nVeterans Home Loan\nVoting & Elections\nWeather\nPublic Records\nBirth & Death Records\nMarriage Certificates\nMilitary Discharge Records\nPassports\nReal Estate\nVeterans Services\nVisiting\nCalendar\nCommunities\nCounty Maps\nNews\nParks & Recreation\nPublic Records\nPayments & Fees\nOnline Payment Options\nCareer Opportunities\nEmployment & Internships\nDrivers License/Passports\nCheck if Appointment is Required\nMapping\nGIS Applications\nProperty Taxes\nPay Property Taxes\nParks & Recreation\nOutdoor Recreation\n-->\nMission: \"To provide accessible and cost-effective services to support quality of life for the Sherburne County community.\"\nContact Us\nSherburne County Government Center\n13880 Business Center Drive NW\nSuite 100\nElk River, MN 55330-4668\nPhone: 763-765-3000\nFaceboo